<DocsLayout title="Haft v9 uses independent capabilities" description="This compatibility page explains why the old five-stage workflow is not the v9 product model.">
  <h1>The old five modes are gone</h1>

  <div class="callout-warn">
    <p>
      <strong>This URL is kept for old links.</strong> v9 does not require
      <code>Understand → Explore → Choose → Execute → Verify</code>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    Real engineering questions do not always begin at the same stage or need
    the same result. Haft v9 exposes independent capabilities and chooses by
    the situation in front of the agent.
  </p>

  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Situation</th><th>Capability</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>The right route is unclear</td><td><code>h-reason</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>The problem is unclear</td><td><code>h-frame</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>A failure has rival causes</td><td><code>h-diagnose</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Different approaches are needed</td><td><code>h-explore</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Existing options need a fair comparison</td><td><code>h-compare</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>The human directly chooses an option</td><td><code>h-decide</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>An old claim must meet current evidence</td><td><code>h-verify</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Current project attention is the question</td><td><code>h-status</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Setup needs attention</td><td><code>h-onboard</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>The product or software contract is current</td><td><code>h-spec</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>One observation should be remembered</td><td><code>h-note</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>A runner needs durable execution authority</td><td><code>h-commission</code></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>
    Ordered plans and methods still exist when the work itself has an order.
    The documentation menu and skill list do not invent that order for every
    project.
  </p>

  <p>
    Most local reasoning can stay in the conversation. A plan is not performed
    work, a recommendation is not a human decision, and a decision is not
    execution authority.
  </p>

  <h2>Next</h2>

  <ul>
